    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499">

                <pb facs="0547" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/1173</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Gonzales
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 302</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 422
                    of the 28th ultimo in which you enclose a translation of a letter addressed to
                    you by General José Miguel Gómez, styled President of the Liberal Directory and
                    General Commanding the Constitutional Army.</p>
                <pb facs="0548" n="382" xml:id="pg382"/>
                <p>It appears to the Department that you need not reply to General Gómez’s
                    letter.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
